MVC : Model, View and Controller 
--> MVC is a way of dividing a web application into 
    Controller (handles requests), Model (stores data), and View (shows data),
    making applications easier to build and maintain.

Model Stores data.
example :
Student
Employee
Product
--> addAttribute()? : addAttribute() is used to add data into the Model object.
    Syntax : model.addAttribute("key", value);

Controller Handles requests.
example :
/home
/login
/register
